.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-wait - Block until a payment settles (or reaches a given status)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments wait  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Poll a payment until it settles, then print its final state.

.PP
By default it waits until no transaction is still in flight (submitted, or signed
and pending broadcast). A prepare that was never signed is not in flight — nothing
will ever send it — so it does not hold the wait open.
With --until it instead waits for a specific payment status, and stops with an
error as soon as the payment can no longer reach it — a charge-mode payment never
becomes 'captured', a captured one never becomes 'authorized' again.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for wait

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=15m0s
	Max time to wait — the default covers the slowest chain's finality

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	Wait until the payment reaches this status (unsigned, signed, authorized, partially_captured, captured, charged, voided, released, refunded, expired)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments wait 0xrail0Id…
  rail0 payments wait 0xrail0Id… --until captured
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
